     My questions was:
     
     >      I am looking for help:
     >      1) How can I create UFS filesystem on /dev/fd0a - 1.44 MB ? >   
     >      2) Can I boot my OSF/1 from /dev/fd0a.
     >      I am working at  Digital Unix 3.2 and 4.0 > 
     >      Any help welcome !
     
     Answer is:
     
     1- create a UFS filesystem on /dev/fd0a
     a - format the floppy 
     /sbin/fddisk -fmt -f /dev/rfd0a
     b- make a label
     /sbin/disklabel -wr /dev/rfd0c rx26
     c- create the filesystem
     /sbin/newfs /dev/rfd0a
     2- Booting from /dev/fd0a
     
     Booting from floppy is possible but answer from Digital is more 
     complicated as my wife :-))
     
