Greetings - 

This is an important message to users of the ZUAUSR utilities
which I have created and have been maintaining. 

If you have v1.14 installed, note that it is a test release 
and v1.15 (available via ftp://raven.alaska.edu/pub/randy/zuausr/)
has patches to correct some bugs which I found in the v1.14 
code when I validated and verified the new features.

I advise skipping the v1.14 release and going straight to the
v1.15 release.

To those of you unaware of what the ZUAUSR utilities are, they 
are command line utilities created to perform account maintenance
under Digital UNIX Enhanced Security (C2 level) levels.  The 
utilities come as a setld installable package complete with 
source, man pages, and an administrator's guide.

The utilities are designed with a locally configurable 
tiered structured to allow pushing account maintenance 
away from the System Administrators and Security Officers.
Of course, there is full auditing performed on all actions
attempted.

These utilities include account creation, locking, reporting, 
unlocking, listing, modification, and expiring (passwords).

Enjoy!


