From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Jan 22 06:55:34 1997
From: Daniel.Clar () supelec ! fr (Daniel Clar)
Date: Wed, 22 Jan 1997 06:55:34 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary : support of LN17ps and number-up on Digital UNIX
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076450423330

In fact, there were two separate questions :

1) is the LN17ps supported by Digital UNIX ?

2) why -Nx option is not supported by Digital UNIX ?


1) The answer at the first question is NO . In a next release, there will be a 
partial support for the LN17ps (see the next answer).

2) The -N option is supported only for printservers. If I try to use lpspr 
and redicrect to the LN17ps , the printer doesn't understand all the 
postscript commands. The -N option is supported on Ultrix and I'm able to 
print to an HPIV SI/Mx printer from Ultrix with all the options.

It's quite a pity to see that OpenVMS engineering has done the effort to 
support very quickly the LN17ps printer with DCPS and that for UNIX it was 
not the case and furthermore that filters and other programs ignore the -N 
option.

I think, I'll continue to buy non-Digital laserprinters.

Daniel


