From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Jan 08 19:02:26 1997
From: John Lucak <JLucak () mr ! picker ! com>
Date: Wed, 08 Jan 1997 19:02:26 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: EV56 Instructions
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076450423042

I've been bugging my Digital sales rep for several months
for this answer. This group provided the answer in under 30 
minutes!

To enable the use of byte/word instructions on an EV56 processor,
use the switch:

       -arch ev56

Processor specific tuning for this architecture can be selected
using 

       -tune ev56

-arch is not documented in the man page (DU 4.0a). -tune is 
documented and although ev56 is not listed, it does work.

Special thanks to Vipin Gokhale  <VGOKHALE@us.oracle.com>
for the speedy response.

