To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY:Adding an IBM disk to DEC Alpha
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076450422967


Hello Managers,

My original question was
"How to add an IBM disk to our system?"

The following people responded to my question. Thanks for all answers.

Christophe Colle <ccolle@office.innet.be>
Gert Maaskant <gertm@cvi.ns.nl>
Sam Sarasin <sarasin@cop.dec.com>
Robert L. McMillin <rlm@syseca-us.com>
Thomas Leitner <tom@finwds01.tu-graz.ac.at>
Tugrul Yilmaz <tugrul@heraklit.physics.metu.edu.tr>
Mr. Dustin Fu <xxfdh@omega.uta.edu>
pat@krl.caltech.edu
Tom Rioux <rioux@ip6480nl.ce.utexas.edu>
Alan Rollow <alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com>


The solution was:

1) Create device files in /dev directory
cd dev
./MAKEDEV rz2
2) add a disklabel to the device.
disklabel -w -r /dev/rrz2c IBMDISK

After these steps, new file domain and file set can be created using
mkfdmn and mkfset commands. (We are using Advanced File System)

Thanks.

--------------------------
Zehra Soysert 
Ege University
soysert@bornova.ege.edu.tr
--------------------------

