Thanks to 

  Hans Ullitz-Moeller <hum@biobase.dk>
 "Muller, Ronald" <Ronald.Muller@metrokc.gov>
  alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com
 "Michael A. Crowley" <mcrowley@mtholyoke.edu>

My question is:
   There are some file whose name's first character is '-'.
How can I read and delete them?

Answer:
  1. You can put double - (--) before file name to read and delete them.
         e.g.:
           #more -- -u
           #rm -- -u
  2. put ./ as prefix to the file name.
         e.g.:
           #more ./-u
            #rm ./-u

W. Peng
